Hisense A6L r5 review fixes F6/F7/F62 (28 Sep 2026) for the AOSP AIDL example audio HAL (ModulePrimary):
  - publishes Android's call devices (Telephony Rx/Tx HW patches, or the legacy primary-output routing while
    AudioMode is IN_CALL) in vendor.a6l.audio.call_out / call_in for a6l-audio-route and a6l-q6voiced
    (speakerphone = TFA9894 via TERT_MI2S voice route; bt-sco reported but unsupported by the routing daemon),
  - F62: publishes Android's ordinary playback/capture devices in every mode (vendor.a6l.audio.media_out, e.g.
    speaker|earpiece|headset|headphone or "speaker,headset"; vendor.a6l.audio.media_in main|headset), which
    a6l-audio-route applies when no modem call is active (VoIP speakerphone, capture from the built-in mic),
  - setMicMute goes to a6l-q6voiced (kernel "VoiceMMode1 TX Mute"), the same state as IRadioVoice.setMute.
Applied in hardware/interfaces by tools/rom-v2-pipeline.sh (audio/patches/*.patch).

